NEW = [
    ("p:sg-decides", "On a topic with a study group, rival designs are first polled there, among those who chose that room over the rooms meeting with it. The design it sends on is where the design room starts, and the design room, which owns selecting designs, can still poll a rival that has a paper.", "split in two"),
    ("l:sg-purpose", "SD-4 has the convenor form a study group on a design room chair's recommendation when a topic has broad interest, no unified initial proposal, and a strong chair candidate. It gives the study group the role of producing an initial proposal that can then enter the design room.", "split in two"),
    ("p:sg-sponsor", "Paying participants to attend a study group puts a sponsor's voters where the design the design room starts from is chosen. In a room with fewer voters, fewer paid participants make up a third of the Favor-plus-Against votes, enough to block, or over two thirds, enough to meet the norm.", ""),
    ("p:deadlock", "When each of two groups casts at least a third of the Favor-plus-Against votes against the other's design, neither design meets the 2:1 norm. The deadlock lasts until voters change position, a design changes, the voters present change, a chair calls consensus below the norm, or the design room sends both to competing TSs.", "'ends only when ... unless' is 'lasts until', the same five exits"),
    ("l:hold-yield-both-hold", "When both groups hold and the deadlock ends with either design equally likely, each can expect half its stake on average, less its cost of holding through it. Members whose costs sponsors pay bear less of that cost per meeting.", "split in two"),
    ("l:hold-yield-half-over-deadlock", "Each group does better when both yield to a compromise worth half its stake than when both hold. That holds because a deadlock both hold brings half its stake on average, less a cost of holding.", "split in two; 'since' becomes 'That holds because'"),
    ("l:hold-yield-cheap-holds", "A group whose cost of holding is less than half its stake does better holding through a deadlock both hold than yielding while the other holds. That holds because half its stake on average, less that cost, leaves it better off than none of its stake.", "split in two; 'since' becomes 'That holds because'"),
    ("l:hold-yield-costly-yields", "A group whose cost of holding is more than half its stake does better yielding while the other holds than holding through a deadlock both hold. That holds because half its stake on average, less that cost, leaves it worse off than none of its stake.", "split in two; 'since' becomes 'That holds because'"),
    ("p:chair-threshold", "Every consensus call has a cost: declaring consensus over Against votes risks later national body opposition, and declining delays work SD-4 says subgroup polls should favor. Departing from the 2:1 norm can cost the caller's post: chairs serve at the convenor's choice with no fixed term, and the convenor for terms SC22 may decline to renew.", "'can also cost' is 'can cost', after the first sentence's costs"),
    ("p:chair-default", "Above the 2:1 line after discussion, declaring consensus follows SD-4's norm, though a Neutral majority can be concerning, and at or below it SD-4 allows a re-poll after discussion. A chair whose stake is worth less than what departing can cost makes the call the norm gives.", "'after the Against voters' concerns are discussed' is 'after discussion', the same discussion the 2:1 norm names"),
    ("l:call-above", "A design room chair whose stake is worth less than what departing can cost ranks declaring consensus above declining or re-polling on a count above 2:1 after discussion. This holds when Neutral votes are not a majority of those voting.", "split in two; the Neutral condition moves to the second sentence"),
    ("l:call-below", "On a count at or below 2:1 after discussion, such a chair ranks declining or re-polling above declaring consensus.", "'not above' is 'at or below'"),
    ("p:chair-confidence", "Of two papers otherwise alike, a chair does better taking up first the one whose author has a record of following procedures and responding to review, which promises fewer problems. That record comes only from taking part.", ""),
    ("p:private-channel", "A participant who thinks a new proposal should not take up extended subgroup time can tell the chair privately and in advance. The chair may then time-box it and poll whether to go on, and nothing in SD-4 requires a record of the request.", "same clauses, regrouped"),
    ("p:plenary-ratifies", "At plenary, design stays with the design rooms, objections not escalated in time get no weight, and all present are asked for serious design concerns. Most polls pass by unanimous consent, and when opposition is significant the convenor usually asks whether Against votes are personal or national body positions.", "'design is left to the design rooms' is 'design stays with the design rooms'"),
]
